<<~ ahu #/bearing>>
! Art Sigils — Procedure Grammar

The portable Inscription carries **one Lares sharktooth `<<~ art ...>>` invocation**, without a procedure declaration. This meme holds the canonical definition and the three optional extensions. The Lararium memetic-wikitext layer owns `<<~ ...>>` dispatch; the receiving wiki needs the corresponding definitions/bindings in scope. An image model may interpret the invocation directly without executing the wiki. Neither reception path guarantees identical results. The 1,024-character target covers the invocation alone, excluding wrappers, reference registers and Folio.

The art-house lexicons live in the semantic specification and **inside values**, not in one procedure per artistic term. Only independently meaningful structural scopes warrant extended procedures. The 1,024-character target applies to the complete **invocation alone**, excluding the source code fence, meme wrapper, reference register and Folio.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/inscription>>
!! Canonical `~art` procedure

The following definition governs the `<<~ art ...>>` Inscription and Folio calls. It stays in this grammar meme rather than in the transmitted artwork. House procedure declarations retain TW5's colon plus double-quoted defaults (`worktype:"artwork"`); invocations use equals plus quoted values (`subject="..."`). Plain TW5 may parse the sharktooth as a call to `~` without providing its Lares meaning; the memetic-wikitext layer supplies that dispatch.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure ~art(worktype:"artwork" subject read imagery:"follow subject and read" treatment:"suit the read" composition:"serve the read" relation:"where meaningful" depiction-scope:"follow worktype and imagery") <<worktype>>: <<subject>>. Read: <<read>>. Imagery: <<imagery>>. Treatment: <<treatment>>. Composition: <<composition>>. Relation: <<relation>>. Depiction scope: <<depiction-scope>>.
```

* The eight semantic dimensions: worktype, subject, read, imagery, treatment, composition, relation, depiction-scope. Procedure definitions use `name:"default"`; house calls use `name="literal value"` (or another TW5 quoted literal form when needed). Supplied values override defaults. Preserve the separate syntaxes.
* `subject` and `read` carry no explicit default; the authoring convention strongly prefers both. Other fields offer neutral or delegating defaults. Blank/silent values remain possible but the compact transclusion may then emit an empty label; do not mistake a blank for a creative instruction.
* A declaration default such as `composition:"serve the read"` supplies literal words for transclusion; a human or model interprets the artistic invitation. A literal value such as `subject="an artist's passage"` preserves its apostrophe; for embedded double quotes use a supported alternative literal delimiter such as `[[...]]`.
* The declared defaults invite artistic freedom: omitted imagery follows subject and read, treatment suits the read, composition serves the read, relation arises only where meaningful, and scope follows worktype and imagery. Explicit values take precedence.
* The procedure's subject and read do not prescribe genre, palette, medium, figures or photographic style. Context may deepen the *reading*, never secretly transplant source metadata as image content.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/folio-modules>>
!! Optional Folio procedures — scoped artistic extensions

The eight-dimension `art()` call handles the artistic nucleus. A Folio can speak with ordinary art-house vocabulary in those same parameter values. The following three procedures offer **optional**, named scopes only when a separate investigation, consequential comparison or material condition merits independent expression.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure ~art-study(question form proposal status:"unresolved") Study: <<question>>. Work: <<form>>. Proposal: <<proposal>>. Status: <<status>>.
\procedure ~art-counterpoint(first second tension evidence:"visible in the images") Counterpoint: <<first>> meets <<second>>; <<tension>>. Evidence: <<evidence>>.
\procedure ~art-facture(scope support medium handling:"let the medium's behavior remain visible") Facture in <<scope>>: <<medium>> on <<support>>; <<handling>>.
```

* **`art-study`:** one interpretable proposal or question explored through a picture, object, variation or experiment. `status` can hold a provisional, rejected, open or settled artistic position without claiming verified fact.
* **`art-counterpoint`:** a consequential relation between two images, passages, concepts, gestures, materials or hypotheses. The `evidence` value names visible or experiential features that give a viewer grounds to compare them. Mere adjacency does not establish opposition.
* **`art-facture`:** medium, support and handling in a specific work or region. Distinguish its physical surface from any object, substance or texture *depicted* within it. No medium or material becomes a default across unrelated parts.

A Folio invokes these procedures only where an independent artistic question, consequential counterpoint or material condition benefits from its own scope. A portrait, an all-over painting, a photograph or a temporal installation may invoke only `art()`. Other artistic vocabulary belongs within parameter values.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/compositional-contract>>
!! Composition, relation, and nested artistic scope

Let the nucleus name **what artwork the maker proposes**. Elaborate only the dimensions whose pictorial or experiential work benefits from more space.

* **Composition** establishes position, rhythm, emphasis, cropping, sequence and interval. **Relation** asks what one part does to another, whether through echo, contrast, erasure, repair, quotation, material friction or deliberate noncontact. A pairing alone need not carry conflict.
* **Shared bearings** can make a counterpoint legible: matching contours in a diptych, one repeated portrait gesture, a motif reprinted at a different scale, a fold continuing across a seam, or a shape transformed in a second material. Choose anchors relevant to the worktype rather than a fixed visual recipe.
* **Study** may explore options or ask what viewers could infer; no artwork must disclose the maker's preliminary drafts.
* **Facture** names where the outer work's support, ground and marks act, as distinct from represented flesh, metal, fabric, stone or digital surface.
* **Nested depiction** separates a physical artwork from the pictures and figures portrayed inside it; address and reference do not automatically count as depicted participants.
* **Silence and openness** can perform the work that an additional procedure would only explain. Delegated parameters permit informed interpretation without filling every slot.
* **Engine controls** and attached sources sit outside the art grammar unless the artwork expressly concerns them. The `~art` procedure articulates consistent dimensions in a Lares-enabled receiver; the invocation alone does not install or register a handler.

The extended procedures provide modular **ways of telling**, not mandatory steps in production, a universal artwork layout, or proof of the artist's intent.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/sample>>
!! Generic use — abstract textile diptych

The following example deliberately leaves maps, genre illustration and studio boards aside. One artistic read unifies a two-panel material work and three optional elaborations.

```tiddlywiki
<<~ art worktype="abstract textile diptych" subject="two incompatible rhythms" read="contact without merger" imagery="a densely stitched field beside a broad painted wash" treatment="raw flax, indigo pigment and irregular thread" composition="unequal panels divided by a quiet interval" relation="loose threads cross the seam yet never join the fields" depiction-scope="only the textile work; no maker depicted">>
<<~ art-study question="Can the gap carry visual tension?" form="two spare panel-spacing trials" proposal="the smallest interval retains palpable separation" status="open">>
<<~ art-counterpoint first="repeated tightly sewn stitches" second="one diffuse blue pigment wash" tension="rhythm meets dispersion" evidence="thread ends cross toward the adjacent field but stop short">>
<<~ art-facture scope="left panel" support="coarse undyed flax" medium="waxed cotton thread and chalk" handling="uneven needle spacing, exposed knots and worn edges">>
```

Load/bind the house procedure definitions in a Lares-enabled wiki before rendering these calls. Plain TW5 inherits the syntax but not the Lararium dispatch. This example demonstrates expressive portability without imposing requirements on other artworks.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/technical-art-example>>
!! Optional technical-art Inscription — specialist example

The same eight fields can articulate a genuinely isolated, transparent FX plate without inventing an additional procedure. A single image-facing call names the intended VISUAL result; actual generation flags, reference inputs, exact dimensions and alpha verification belong to the receiver/compositing notes described in [[Technical-Art Plate Fieldcraft|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/technical-art]].

```tiddlywiki
<<~ art worktype="transparent RGBA technical-art FX plate" subject="several detached luminous vapor wisps" read="scattered breaths of gentle light in open space" imagery="six small pale-violet mist curls, sparse gold and turquoise pinlights, a few hair-fine streamers" treatment="feathered watercolor translucency, restrained local bloom" composition="wide shallow strip, asymmetric separate islands, most canvas clear alpha; a few trails bleed at edges" relation="wind right-to-left and slightly down, warm sun rim from upper-right, cool opposite fill" depiction-scope="FX marks only, no bodies, scenery, panels or captions">>
```

A second distinct plate for organism bodies would have its own call and independent generated output; it is not a request for a two-panel sheet. A tool's actual transparent-background flag is external receiver control, not a ninth Art Sigil argument. The example sets no universal palette, anatomy or fixed plate dimensions.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/notation-contract>>
!! Procedure declaration, invocation and delegation

* Canonical declarations use colon plus double-quoted defaults, e.g. `worktype:"artwork"` and `treatment:"suit the read"`.
* Lares sharktooth calls use equals plus quoted `name="value"` parameters for the `~art` nucleus and all optional procedures. The host's TW5 parameter grammar supplies the literal value forms; use `[[...]]` or single quotes when an embedded double quote requires a different delimiter.
* Apostrophes within double-quoted values survive as literal text. Double quotes within a value need another supported literal delimiter; quotation marks that survive substitution may influence an image receiver's text-rendering conventions.
* Omitted parameters inherit declared defaults verbatim. The receiving artist or model, not TW5, decides how to interpret their artistic delegation.
* A default-free missing argument can yield empty output rather than an instruction to invent content. Keep portable Inscription values literal; context-dependent substitutions, where supported, require their own explicit scope.
* An artwork-specific Inscription carries one sharktooth invocation; its surrounding meme may include a literal-rendering reference and a link to this grammar. The invocation by itself does not bind a house sigil inside an otherwise unconfigured wiki.
<<~/ahu>>
<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>
!! Aftermath — meaning across representation

The written house call, its literal transclusion and the resulting artwork carry related but distinct meanings. A receiving artist's unexpected pictorial choices invite interpretation; they do not silently add parameters to the Art Sigil.

A support, motif, genre, material convention, named artist or depicted subject belongs to the artistic invitation that names it. The eight-dimensional nucleus and three optional Folio procedures impose no house style, narrative format or image layout.
<<~/ahu>>
<<~ ahu #/tw5-source>>
